# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY (2026-09-21): the v0.4.6 snapshot is meant to be deployed on a Linux VPS with
# `chmod +x install.sh && ./install.sh`. Git on Windows warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF",
# and a shell script checked out with CRLF dies on Linux with
# `bash: ./install.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory`.
# Force LF for shell scripts so a clone on any platform yields a runnable installer.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers keep CRLF (cmd.exe / PowerShell are happiest with it).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
